# Appendix B, part 2: writing, the panels, the older file, the fonts file,
# search paths, start, what is not configuration.
.h2 When and how the settings are written [appcfg-write]
.ix Saving the settings
.ix Writing the settings
.ix Cannot write
.h3 Which action writes what [appcfg-write-when]
.table 26 34
Action | What is written
Setup accepted in the Document Manager | {c:config}, all its lines.  These
 | come from the panel ({c:print_to}, {c:print_queue}, {c:pdf_dir}, {c:spell_language},
 | workdir, the Editor, autosave, {c:autosave_seconds}, {c:x11_rows}, {c:terminal_rows},
 | {c:terminal_charset}, {c:default_paper}, {c:undo_levels}, backups, {c:pdf_viewer}); the others
 | are taken from the file as it is at that moment.
Options accepted in the Editor | {c:config}, all its lines.  Five come from
 | the panel ({k:F12}, Global, Options, Ins); the others are taken from the
 | file as it is at that moment.
The height of a window is changed | One line of
 | {c:config}: {c:x11_rows} after the height has not changed for a second
 | and when the program ends, {c:terminal_rows} when the program ends (see
 | {n:appcfg-key-rows}).  Every other line stays as it is.
A font panel accepted in the Document Manager | {c:fonts}, all twenty lines.
Anything else | Nothing.
.end
A change made in one program is not lost when the other saves.  Cancelling a
panel with {k:Esc} writes nothing.  Edit / Preview / Print Document changes the
Working Directory and the Document Name of the panel for the rest of the
session, but never writes {c:config}.
A failed write of the height of a window is no failure of the program: the
height is used until the program ends, and nothing is shown on the screen;
the reason is in the log of the run ({n:appcfg-log}).
.note The Editor never changes {c:autosave} or {c:autosave_seconds}; the
  Options panel has no field for them.  They are set in the Setup panel of
  the Document Manager only.
.h3 Messages of a failed write [appcfg-write-errors]
.ix Settings, error messages
.table 31 29
Message | Cause
There is no home directory | No {c:STRATA_HOME}, no {c:HOME}, and no
 | home directory for the user.
Cannot make DIR: REASON | The directory is not there and could not be
 | made (permission, a missing parent).
DIR is not a directory of yours | The directory is a link, a file, or
 | belongs to another user (see
 | {n:appcfg-dir-checks}).
Cannot write FILE: REASON | The file could not be written (the
 | disk is full, no permission).
.end
In the Document Manager a failed save of {c:config} shows the pop-up Setup with
the text "Settings are in effect but could not be saved": the new values are used until the
program ends, and the reason is not shown.  In the Editor the message above is
the text of a pop-up titled Options.  A failed save of {c:fonts} shows the
message in a pop-up titled Fonts (see {n:str-fonts}).  A font with a bad
character is refused before anything is written (see
{n:appcfg-fonts-rules}).
.h2 The Setup panel and the keys [appcfg-setup]
.ix Setup panel, keys
.ix Setup, validation
.ix Settings not saved
The fields of the Setup panel of the Document Manager that are settings of the
user are listed here (see {n:str-setup} for the panel).  This table gives the
connection between the fields and the keys, and the checks made when the
panel is accepted.
.table 17 14 28
Field | Key | Check when the field is left, and on Ins
Print To | {c:print_to} | A choice of Printer, File only and PDF viewer
 | | (saved as printer, file or viewer); Printer is not offered when the
 | | system has no queue, and a saved Printer is kept.
Printer Queue | {c:print_queue} | A choice from the queues of the system
 | | (System default is saved as no line); a saved queue that is not
 | | listed now is kept.
PDF Directory | {c:pdf_dir} | Empty, a full path or {c:~/} and a path, else the
 | | reason "The PDF Directory is a full path or
 | | starts with {c:~/}" is shown at the foot.  A
 | | directory that does not exist is saved.
Paper for New Documents | {c:default_paper} | A choice of Letter and A4.
 | | Letter is saved as no line, A4 as {c:a4}.  The file
 | | may have {c:letter} or {c:a4}; another word is
 | | ignored.
Dictionary Language | {c:spell_language} | Letters, digits and _ - @ only, else the
 | | reason "The Dictionary Language is a code
 | | such as en_US or de_DE".
Initial Working Directory | workdir | May be empty.  Otherwise it must
 | | be an existing directory, else the reason
 | | "The initial working directory does not
 | | exist".
Editor program | stred | No check.  Used as typed.  See
 | | {x:str-find-editor}.
Autosave | autosave | A choice of Yes and No.  A settings file
 | | may have yes or no in any case of letters.
Autosave Interval (Seconds) | {c:autosave_seconds} | A number from 1 to 86400
 | | ({c:90s} is 90), else the reason "The
 | | autosave interval is 1 to 86400 seconds".
Window Rows, X11 | {c:x11_rows} | Empty, or a whole number, else the
 | | reason "The window rows are a whole number,
 | | or empty".  A number below
 | | 20 is saved as 20 and above 200 as 200; 50
 | | is saved as no line.
Window Rows, Terminal | {c:terminal_rows} | The same.  Empty is saved as no
 | | line.  The two fields are one line of the panel.
Terminal Characters | {c:terminal_charset} | One of four choices, so no check.
 | | Automatic is saved as no line, UTF-8 as {c:utf8},
 | | ASCII as {c:ascii}.
Undo Levels (0 to 500) | {c:undo_levels} | A whole number, else the reason "Undo
 | | Levels is a whole number from 0 to 500".  A number above 500 is
 | | saved as 500; 100 is saved as no line.
Backups Kept (0 to 99) | backups | A whole number, else the reason "Backups
 | | Kept is a whole number from 0 to 99".  A number above 99 is saved as
 | | 99; 1 is saved as no line.
PDF Viewer | {c:pdf_viewer} | A full path (letters, digits and . _ + - /
 | | only), else the reason "The PDF viewer needs its full
 | | path, such as {c:/usr/bin/evince}".  Empty is saved as no line.  A word
 | | processor gives the reason "A word processor is not a PDF viewer".
 | | A file that is not executable or not safe is refused too.
Screen Colors | the color keys | The second page of the panel; {k:Ins} keeps
 | | its colors with the other pages, and every color that
 | | is chosen is checked ({n:appcfg-key-colors}).
.end
A field is checked when the focus leaves it and all the fields are checked
when {k:Ins} is pressed.  A wrong value keeps the panel open: the focus is in
that field, the reason is shown in bold in the line at the foot, and every
other value that was typed is kept; {k:Esc} throws the panel away.  On
success the new values are in effect at once, the file is written, and the
footer shows "Settings saved to {c:PATH}" with the full path of {c:config}.
The third page, the advanced settings, has the Initial Macro Set, the Initial
Library, Terminal Characters, the Editor program and the Help File; {k:PgUp}
and {k:PgDn} go from page to page, and {k:Ins} on any page keeps all of them.
.pic pictures/str-setup-panel.png 5 The Setup panel.
.h2 The Options panel and the keys [appcfg-options]
.ix Options panel, keys
.ix Global, Options, settings
The panel is opened with {k:F12}, Global, Options.  The rows that are
settings of the user are these.
.table 19 14 26
Row | Key | Notes
Expanded Status Line? | {c:expanded_status} | [Yes] or [No].
Display On-Screen Help? | {c:onscreen_help} | [Yes] or [No].
Display Tab & End-of-Line | {c:show_marks} | [Yes] or [No].
 Characters? | |
Display Dots for Spaces? | {c:show_dots} | [Yes] or [No].
Backups Kept (0 to 99) | backups | A whole number, else the pop-up "Backups
 | | Kept is a whole number from 0 to 99".  A number
 | | above 99 is saved as 99; 1 is saved as no line.
.end
{k:Ins} accepts: the new values are in effect on the screen at once, and
{c:config} is written (see {n:appcfg-write}).  {k:Esc} cancels.  The panel
shows the values that the running Editor has, which it read from the file at
start; so a change made to {c:config} by hand while the Editor runs is not
seen until the Editor is started again, and is lost if the Options panel is
accepted.
.pic pictures/edit-b-options.png 5 The Options panel of the Editor.
.h2 The older settings file [appcfg-legacy]
.ix Older settings file
.ix strata.conf
.ix XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Earlier versions of Strata kept the settings in a file {c:strata.conf} in the
directory {c:strata} under the configuration directory of the desktop
({c:.config} in the home directory).  The file has the same lines as
{c:config}.  It is read only when there is no settings directory yet.  The
first save (Setup or Options) writes a new {c:config} with its values, and the
older file has no more effect; it is never changed or removed.
.if .STRATA_BUILD_TYPE # release
For developers: the directory is the one named by the environment variable
{c:XDG_CONFIG_HOME} when it is set and not empty.  The older file is read in
these cases only.
.table 34 26
Condition | Result
{c:STRATA_HOME} is set | The older file is never read.
{c:STRATA_HOME} is not set and the | The older file is read.
 settings directory does not exist, or has |
 no {c:config} that can be opened |
{c:config} exists | The older file is ignored, whatever it holds.
The settings directory or {c:config} is | Defaults.  The older file is not
 not used (see {n:appcfg-dir-checks}) | read.
.end
If neither {c:HOME} nor {c:XDG_CONFIG_HOME} is set, no older file is looked
for.
.endif
.h2 The font list [appcfg-fonts]
.ix fonts file
.ix Font list file
.ix TeX Font Association, file
.ix Font numbers
A font of a document is a number (1 Headline, 2 Text, 3 Header/Footer, 4 to 20
the other fonts).  The file {c:fonts} in the settings directory says which
LaTeX font each number stands for.  It is made and changed by the TeX Font
Association entry of the Document Manager (see {n:str-fonts}).  The Document
Manager shows the list; the Editor uses it for the labels of font numbers in
the Typeface and Keycap panels ("Text (Latin Modern Roman)").  The rules of
{x:appcfg-dir} apply to the file.
.h3 Format of the file [appcfg-fonts-format]
.ix Font file format
One line for each font, seven fields separated by a bar:
.code
NUMBER|NAME|PACKAGE|OPTIONS|FAMILY|ARCHIVE|MAP
5|Helvetica|helvet|scaled=0.92|sans||
19|Lato|lato|default|sans|lato|lato.map
.end
.table 12 48
Field | Meaning
NUMBER | The font number, 1 to 20.
NAME | The name that the panels show (Palatino).  Any text without a bar.
PACKAGE | The LaTeX package that selects the font, or empty for the
 | fonts that LaTeX has without a package (Computer Modern).
OPTIONS | The options of the package ({c:scaled=0.92}), or empty.
FAMILY | roman, sans or mono: the kind of the font.
ARCHIVE | The name of the archive on CTAN that holds the font, or empty.
MAP | The map file to enable after the archive is installed, or empty.
.end
.h3 How the file is read and written [appcfg-fonts-rules]
.ix Font file rules
.ix Font entry, invalid character
.table 24 36
Rule | Effect
Start | The list of defaults (next section) is loaded first, then
 | the file changes the entries it names.
A line with other than seven fields | Ignored.
A number outside 1 to 20, a family | Ignored; the default of that number
 other than the three words, or a | stays.
 character not allowed in PACKAGE, |
 OPTIONS, ARCHIVE or MAP |
Allowed characters | Letters, digits and the signs . _ - + = ,
 | in PACKAGE, OPTIONS, ARCHIVE and MAP; any
 | character but a bar in NAME.
Several lines for one number | The last one wins.
Writing | All twenty lines are written, in order of
 | number.  The file therefore holds the defaults
 | too once any font was changed.
Refused write | "Font N has a character that cannot be used
 | (only letters, digits and . _ - + = , are allowed)".
.end
.h3 The list that Strata comes with [appcfg-fonts-defaults]
.ix Default fonts
.ix Font defaults
A user who has no file, or no line for a number, has these fonts.
.table 4 20 11 9 9
No. | Name | Package | Options | Family
1 | Latin Modern Sans | lmodern | | sans
2 | Latin Modern Roman | lmodern | | roman
3 | Latin Modern Roman | lmodern | | roman
4 | Times | mathptmx | | roman
5 | Helvetica | helvet | scaled=0.92 | sans
6 | Courier | courier | | mono
7 | Palatino | mathpazo | | roman
8 | Bookman | bookman | | roman
9 | New Century Schoolbook | newcent | | roman
10 | Avant Garde | avant | | sans
11 | Zapf Chancery | chancery | | roman
12 | Charter | charter | | roman
13 | Utopia | utopia | | roman
14 | TeX Gyre Termes | tgtermes | | roman
15 | TeX Gyre Heros | tgheros | | sans
16 | TeX Gyre Pagella | tgpagella | | roman
17 | TeX Gyre Cursor | tgcursor | | mono
18 | Computer Modern Roman | (none) | | roman
19 | Lato | lato | default | sans
20 | (empty) | (none) | | roman
.end
Fonts 1 to 18 are fonts that every TeX Live installation has.  Font 19 has the
archive {c:lato} and the map file {c:lato.map}, so it can be installed from
CTAN; font 20 is free for your own choice.  The panels that show a font number
(Typeface list, Format panels, Keycap markers) use the names as labels:
"Headline (Latin Modern Sans)", "Text (...)", "Header/Footer (...)",
"Font 4 (Times)" and so on; an empty name leaves the plain role or number.
.h3 Installing a font from CTAN [appcfg-fonts-install]
.ix CTAN
.ix Install Now
.ix Font download
When Install Now is Yes in the font panel, the Document Manager downloads the
archive of the font from CTAN and installs it in the TeX directory of the
user (usually {c:texmf} in the home directory).  The programs {c:kpsewhich},
{c:curl}, {c:unzip}, {c:mktexlsr} and {c:updmap-user} must be installed; each
step fails with a message in a pop-up.
.table 5 55
Step | Action and failure message
1 | Find the TeX directory of the user.  If TeX does not answer:
 | "kpsewhich did not run (is TeX installed?)".
2 | Download the archive.  The address is
 | {c:https://mirrors.ctan.org/install/fonts/ARCHIVE.tds.zip}.  Failure:
 | "The archive could not be downloaded from ADDRESS".
3 | Unpack it into the TeX directory.  Failure: "The archive could
 | not be unpacked".
4 | Make the file name database of TeX again.
5 | If MAP is not empty, enable the map file.  Failure:
 | "updmap-user failed to enable the map file".
.end
While the steps run, a box titled Installing font names the step that is
running; {k:Esc} stops the download (step 2): the footer shows "Installation
cancelled", the partial file is removed and nothing is installed.  Steps 3 to 5
are short and cannot be stopped.
.if .STRATA_BUILD_TYPE # release
.ix STRATA_CTAN_URL
For developers: when the environment variable {c:STRATA_CTAN_URL} is set and
not empty, the address of step 2 is that value followed by
{c:/ARCHIVE.tds.zip}.
.endif
An entry with no ARCHIVE gives "This font has no archive to download"; an
ARCHIVE or MAP with a bad character, or an ARCHIVE with a slash, gives "The
name of the archive or of the map file has a character that cannot be used".
On success the pop-up shows "Installed in DIRECTORY".  A font counts as
installed when its package is found by TeX; an entry with no package is always
installed.
.h2 Search paths [appcfg-search]
.ix Search paths
.ix Where Strata looks for files
.h3 The Editor [appcfg-search-editor]
.ix Editor search
The setting of the Editor in {c:config}, then the Editor's file next to the
Document Manager's, then the system directories; see {x:str-find-editor}.
.if .STRATA_BUILD_TYPE # release
For developers: the environment variable {c:STRED} comes after the setting.
.endif
.h3 Templates [appcfg-search-templates]
.ix Templates, search
.ix STRATA_TEMPLATES
.ix Template file
A template named in the New command of the Editor (File, New) is looked for
like this.  The comparison of names ignores the case of the letters (Memo.DOC
is found for {c:memo.doc}).
.table 5 55
Step | Place
1 | If the name contains a slash, exactly that path.
2 | The Working Directory of the panel.
3 | The directory named by {c:STRATA_TEMPLATES}, if it is set.
4 | The directory {c:templates} of the settings directory.
5 | The directory {c:share/strata/templates} beside the programs.
6 | The directory of the program file of the Editor.
.end
An installed program needs nothing set: the templates are found beside the
program.
A program run in place from a build directory finds them when the setup
script of the sources has been sourced, which sets {c:STRATA_TEMPLATES}.
The list of templates that New shows is made from the files that end in
{c:.doc} or {c:.set} in the directory named by {c:STRATA_TEMPLATES}, in
{c:templates} below the settings directory, and in {c:share/strata/templates}
of the installation (a name that is in an earlier one hides the same name
in a later one).
If none is found and the name is {c:DEFAULT.SET}, a new document is made from
the built-in default, after asking Structured or Unstructured.  Otherwise the
message "Cannot find the template file" is shown.
.h3 Macro sets and libraries [appcfg-search-macro]
.ix Macro file, search
.ix Library file, search
The File Name that you type for a macro set (extension {c:.mac}) or a library
(extension {c:.lib}) is joined to the Working Directory of the panel, unless
it begins with a slash; an extension is added when the name has no dot.
.h3 Helper programs [appcfg-search-programs]
.ix Printer, search
.ix Viewer, search
When the Editor needs another program of Strata (Draft, Final and Preview need
the Printer, and Preview needs the Viewer) the program is found like this.
.table 5 55
Step | Place
1 | The directory of the program file of the Editor.
2 | The system directories ({n:appcmd-find}).
.end
.if .STRATA_BUILD_TYPE # release
.ix STRATA_STRPRINT
.ix STRATA_DVIVIEW
For developers: before step 1 the environment variable {c:STRATA_STRPRINT} or
{c:STRATA_DVIVIEW} is looked at, if it is set and not empty.  It must name a
program that can be run; if it does not, the program is not found: no further
search is made.
.endif
The programs that the Printer runs ({c:pdflatex}, {c:latex}, {c:dvipdfmx},
{c:gs}, and the
others of {n:appcmd-external}) are found in the system directories only, never in
{c:PATH}.  The files that they
make while they work are put under {c:TMPDIR} when it is set and not empty,
otherwise in the system directory for such files.
.h3 The cache of equations [appcfg-search-cache]
.ix Equation cache
.ix XDG_CACHE_HOME
.ix Cache directory
The Editor keeps the pictures of equations that it has rendered in a cache,
so that they are not made again.  It is not a setting of the user and is not
in the settings directory.  The directory is {c:strata/eqn} under the
directory named by {c:XDG_CACHE_HOME} if that is set and is an absolute path,
otherwise under {c:.cache} in the home directory.  The cache can be deleted
at any time.
.h2 Settings that are not in the settings directory [appcfg-notin]
.ix Document settings
.ix Settings kept in the document
.ix Global format, where kept
Everything that you set in the Global menu except the five Options of the
table above belongs to the document and is saved with it: the Global Format
and Page panels, the Typeface list (the names of the fonts of the document),
the Marker defaults and the named formats.  The font list of
{x:appcfg-fonts} is different: the list gives
what a font number means to LaTeX for every document of the user,
whereas the document's Typeface list gives the numbers their names.  The
terminal and the window (the X11 font, size and size of the window) are set
by environment variables, listed in {x:appcmd-env}, and not kept anywhere.
.h2 Examples and troubleshooting [appcfg-examples]
.ix Examples, configuration
.ix Troubleshooting, settings
.h3 A settings file for a project directory
.code
workdir=/home/ann/book
autosave=yes
autosave_seconds=60
backups=3
show_dots=yes
.end
The keys that are left out keep their defaults, and the first save from a
panel adds them.
.h3 Trying settings without touching your own
Start the Document Manager with the environment variable {c:STRATA_HOME} set
to a new directory, for example {c:/tmp/try}.  The directory is made at the
first save, and your own settings are not read or changed.
.h3 Problems
.table 26 34
Symptom | Cause and remedy
A setting reverts to its default | The directory or file belongs to someone
 | else (see {n:appcfg-dir-checks}), or the
 | line has a space around the key or the
 | value.
{c:autosave=No} still saves | Only lower case {c:no} and {c:0} mean No.
Setup shows "setting not saved" | A check failed (see {n:appcfg-setup}); nothing
 | was changed.
A hand edit is lost | The Editor was running; all keys are written
 | when Options is accepted.
The Editor path keeps changing | The path is the one that the Document
 | Manager found; it is not saved unless it was typed.
.end
